#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365003 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133789 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c07721dd-4b97-5d57-8de1-5098117e3071" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector Onto a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c8cc9b5-4fea-51be-8530-093f28bb182d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365005} {:answer/id #uuid "d8437765-1667-5b4a-a2d4-519d741042f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365006} {:answer/id #uuid "80156ccd-7acc-5a08-958d-43e718870bf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365007} {:answer/id #uuid "46e97d17-2170-52e4-bae8-f1a4b26c06f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365008} {:answer/id #uuid "bb6446d2-ce20-5814-95a8-6fcf987d8011" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365009}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c8cc9b5-4fea-51be-8530-093f28bb182d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365005} :answer-field/id #uuid "0051ff91-5982-5f79-8021-15f6e5a79345" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365004}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b15ae07d-6779-551f-ab28-55256b58c480" :question/math-academy-id "q-140452" :question/problem "Find the orthogonal projection of the vector $x$ onto the plane $r=sv+tw,$ where $s,t\\in R,$ and\n\n$$\nv=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,w=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $v$ and $w$ are linearly independent. \n\nThe orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nSince our plane passes through the origin, it defines the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{v,w}$ in ${R}^{3}.$ In our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}| & | \\\\ v & w \\\\ | & |\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot {(\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix})}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot {\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365171 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133789 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c07721dd-4b97-5d57-8de1-5098117e3071" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector Onto a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af4b666c-66b7-59db-a2c7-375a67faef78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365173} {:answer/id #uuid "2491dfc4-81ea-5a89-b8be-feb29fe808fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365174} {:answer/id #uuid "1d65e323-bafc-5753-acb8-9ac7daf8900d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365175} {:answer/id #uuid "e5472a7d-a8ec-53cc-922d-6c6d7cc7492e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365176} {:answer/id #uuid "d3b72fcb-1431-51dd-bb92-2f52bbb46be9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365177}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af4b666c-66b7-59db-a2c7-375a67faef78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365173} :answer-field/id #uuid "80f414bd-ce38-5f46-a4ae-f2f0ad8e10ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365172}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4f1a2346-136d-53f7-ba3d-f6d83d0dc1db" :question/math-academy-id "q-158299" :question/problem "Find the orthogonal projection of the vector $x$ onto the plane $r=sv+tw,$ where $s,t\\in R,$ and\n\n$$\nv=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,w=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $v$ and $w$ are linearly independent. \n\nThe orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nSince our plane passes through the origin, it defines the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{v,w}$ in ${R}^{3}.$ In our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}| & | \\\\ v & w \\\\ | & |\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot {(\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix})}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot {\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 9\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\frac{1}{50}\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392354 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133788 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ad9f55b2-ce37-507f-8cb6-7d4e30e6868a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector Onto a Subspace"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74abe4d7-e589-5617-ab73-5aa70c9a7476" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392356} {:answer/id #uuid "ffa1264a-2a73-508f-bc53-ad361bb49d45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392357} {:answer/id #uuid "2a9e59f7-854e-5b73-a998-750da087cf90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392358} {:answer/id #uuid "023b683d-9286-56c1-9880-82005e279d51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392359} {:answer/id #uuid "6a7a2853-3ab5-5f8f-83a3-978af68e4e67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392360}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a7a2853-3ab5-5f8f-83a3-978af68e4e67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392360} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f5082e4-d9ee-539a-9cb4-b5f824bb8ce6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392355}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5c071401-3e46-54b6-b9cb-b8280a1a58b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-40630" :question/problem "Verify whether the vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}$ are linearly independent, and find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the vectors ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we verify whether ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}$ are linearly independent. So, we start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, the pivot columns correspond to the linearly independent vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ that form the basis of our span.\n\nNow, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the linearly independent columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,⇒\\,{A}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot {(\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix})}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot {\\begin{bmatrix}14 & 9 \\\\ 9 & 6\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -9 \\\\ -9 & 14\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
